Wait: using `device->sensor` may be NULL during the rear open? It's set in init_wrap before ischain_init. Good. For the front open, it's front.

But the `gpio_cfg ON` re-run for the front module: the front S_INPUT already ran it, so it may return "already enabled" and re-select pinctrl. It's safe (we did it before). For the front, it also sets reset high. We then force reset.

The rails for the front: check the 5e3 gpio_cfg logs from the front boot:
`VDD_VTCAM_SENSOR_A2P8`, `VDD_VTCAM_1P2`, `VDDIO_1.8V_VT`, and maybe `VDDAF_2.8V_CAM` (the front module may not have AF). If a rail name doesn't exist, regulator_get fails and prints get=-ENODEV; fine.

The probe addresses: for ch1, 0x20 is the front sensor; also test 0x5a. Our info line prints both.

The EEPROM probes: rear EEPROM 0x58 on gpc2; front EEPROM 0x10 on gpf0-2/3. During the front open, the front EEPROM rail VDDIO_1.8V_VT is on; the rear EEPROM rail VDDIO_1.8V_CAM may be off, so rear58 may not ACK. That's fine; the front10 is the self-test.

During the rear open, rear58 ACKs and front10 ACKs (VDDIO_CAM on); good.

