**Found the kernel bug.** In `s2mpu03.c`, when `pdata->g3d_en` is set, the PMIC init runs:

```c
/* sync buck4 and ldo10 */
sec_reg_update(iodev, S2MPU03_REG_L10CTRL, 0x00, 0xC0);
```

That writes **0** into L10CTRL bits [7:6] — the LDO10 enable bits (`0x03 << 6 = 0xC0`) — **after** `regulator_register` already enabled the always-on rail. So the rail is deliberately cleared at PMIC probe, leaving GPS unpowered. Checking whether our DT sets `g3d_en`.

