details.message:
(a) is commissioned from MMLock with your constraints, plus one finding that explains your missing errno.

Root cause of the silent submit error: `p7580_submit_err()` shares the 8-line `p7580_sched_trace` budget (submit.c, `if (p7580_sched_trace && err) { p7580_sched_trace--; pr_info("submit_err stage=%s rc=%ld") }`), and there is no knob to re-arm it — it is a plain static. After the first 8 SUBMITs of a process, any later SUBMIT error prints nothing, so a 300-frame run can never show the assert's errno. I have asked MMLock to give error attribution its own error-only counter (or ratelimited print) in the int48 overlay: log-only, rare, no hot-path cost, and gated so int48 stays acceptance-equivalent when idle.

int48 scope as commissioned:
- overlay patch AFTER driver 0001 (0001 sha stays 04db08d), committing to the repo so patches/ is clean before I build;
- `p7580/prof_arm` debugfs knob, all counters no-ops when unarmed, additive/incremental, print every 100 SUBMITs only while armed;
- the submit_err budget fix above;
- no functional change.

Report will fold in your data: 2/4 ×300 with `Assertion failed: !ret` (pan_job.c:1268) after a silent timeout, one 72 fps run, and the 512² ×30 storm reproduction (MMLock's capture had ev_arm=0, so there is no payload; FpsSplit is being asked to re-run armed).

I am not building until the overlay is committed and `git status` is clean under patches/. Then one build, 31 gates + new prof gates, shas to you.

