{"content": "int48 runtime defect, diagnosed from the flashed image: `p7580/prof_arm` does not exist. `p7580_prof_debugfs_init()` calls `debugfs_create_dir("p7580", NULL)`; that directory is already created by the driver, so the call returns `-EEXIST`, `IS_ERR_OR_NULL` is false (it's an ERR_PTR), and the function returns before creating `prof_arm`. My runs printed `can't create /sys/kernel/debug/p7580/prof_arm: Permission denied` and `ls` confirms only chain_mode/dump/ev_arm/hang_inject/iova_arm/job_timeout_ms/serialize_fs/trace_arm.

Fix in the overlay (int49): reuse the existing root dir — `debugfs_lookup("p7580", NULL)` (or keep a drv field for the dir created by the driver) and create `prof_arm` inside it; on `-EEXIST`-class failure log at `p7580perf:` level, never return silently. Also add a probe-time sanity check so this cannot regress unseen.

Separately for the record, from the flashed int48 (unarmed): 4×300 = 158.8 / 105.8 / 155.5 / 151.4 fps, 0 aborts, 0 ERR/TO; 4×512²×40 readback = 60.6 / 54.9 / 38.3 / 39.8 fps, all clean (no timeouts) — so the 0x08 storm did not reproduce in that window.", "i": "Reporting prof_arm registration bug", "path": "agent://G31_Integrator41"}

